"arguments":{"account_number_last4":"4321"},"exception":null,"result":"{\"account\":{\"id\":1,\"account_type\":\"checking\",\"account_number_last4\":\"4321\",\"account_name\":\"Chase Total Checking\",\"current_balance\":5230.45,\"available_balance\":5230.45,\"currency\":\"USD\"},\"transactions\":[{\"id\":6,\"amount\":41.51,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Grocery Store\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-10T18:20:00\",\"balance_after\":5230.45},{\"id\":5,\"amount\":300.0,\"transaction_type\":\"credit\",\"description\":\"Transfer from Savings\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-07T16:45:00\",\"balance_after\":5271.96},{\"id\":4,\"amount\":200.0,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Electric Bill Payment\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-05T10:00:00\",\"balance_after\":4971.96},{\"id\":3,\"amount\":12.5,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Starbucks\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-03T09:15:00\",\"balance_after\":5171.96},{\"id\":2,\"amount\":45.99,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Amazon Purchase\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-02T14:30:00\",\"balance_after\":5184.46}]}","status":200,"tool_name":"get_account_summary"},{"arguments":{"account_number_last4":"4321"},"exception":null,"result":"{\"account\":{\"id\":1,\"account_type\":\"checking\",\"account_number_last4\":\"4321\",\"account_name\":\"Chase Total Checking\",\"current_balance\":5230.45,\"available_balance\":5230.45,\"currency\":\"USD\"},\"transactions\":[{\"id\":6,\"amount\":41.51,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Grocery Store\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-10T18:20:00\",\"balance_after\":5230.45},{\"id\":5,\"amount\":300.0,\"transaction_type\":\"credit\",\"description\":\"Transfer from Savings\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-07T16:45:00\",\"balance_after\":5271.96},{\"id\":4,\"amount\":200.0,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Electric Bill Payment\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-05T10:00:00\",\"balance_after\":4971.96},{\"id\":3,\"amount\":12.5,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Starbucks\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-03T09:15:00\",\"balance_after\":5171.96},{\"id\":2,\"amount\":45.99,\"transaction_type\":\"debit\",\"description\":\"Amazon Purchase\",\"transaction_date\":\"2024-05-02T14:30:00\",\"balance_after\":5184.46}]}","status":200,"tool_name":"get_account_summary"}],"messages":[{"content":"        # MCP Tools\n\n        You are at a MCP environment. You need to call MCP tools to assist with the user query. You have already logged in, and your user id is 1 if required for the MCP tool.\n\n        You are provided with THREE functions within <tools></tools> XML tags:\n        <tools>\n        1. list_tools\n    - Description: List all available MCP tools in the current environment (name + one-line description only).\n    - Arguments: None\n    - Output: A list of tool names and their one-line descriptions\n\n2. get_tool_detail_of\n    - Description: Get the detailed parameters (input schema) of ONE specific tool. You MUST call this BEFORE calling that tool for the first time, so you never guess its parameters.\n    - Arguments:\n        - tool_name: str, required, the name of the tool you want to inspect\n    - Output: The full input schema (parameters, types, required/optional, descriptions) of that tool\n\n3. call_tool\n    - Description: Call a MCP environment-specific tool\n    - Arguments:\n        - tool_name: str, required, the tool name in the list_tools output\n        - arguments: str, required, the arguments for calling <tool_name>. You must pass a valid JSON string without any markdown fences or additional commentary. This JSON str will be parsed by the tool and executed. You can pass an empty JSON str if no arguments are required by <tool_name>.\n    - Output: The result of the <tool_name> tool call\n        </tools>\n\n        Working rules (IMPORTANT):\n        - You MUST always call list_tools FIRST to discover the available tools, and only call it once.\n        - Before calling a specific tool (call_tool) for the FIRST time, you MUST call get_tool_detail_of for that tool to learn its parameters. Do NOT guess the parameters.\n        - You may call the same tool again later without re-querying its detail.\n\n        In each step, you MUST output EXACTLY ONE of the following two tags:\n\n        1. <awm_tool_call>{\"name\": <function-name>, \"arguments\": <args-json-object>}</awm_tool_call>\n           → Call ONE tool (list_tools / get_tool_detail_of / call_tool). Call only ONE tool per step.\n\n         2. <final_answer>...</final_answer>\n            → Your final answer. Use this ONLY when the task is FULLY completed (and you have no more tools to call).\n            You MUST repeat the requested result inside this tag. The tag is the answer to the user.\n\n        HOW TO CALL A BUSINESS TOOL (call_tool) — WORKED EXAMPLE:\n        - Business tools are called through the SAME \"<awm_tool_call>\" tag. The only difference from list_tools/get_tool_detail_of is that the business tool name and its arguments go INSIDE the \"arguments\" field of call_tool.\n        - call_tool's \"arguments\" field is a JSON **string** (a JSON object serialized as text), so the inner quotes must be escaped.\n        - Example: to call the business tool \"create_applicant\" with {\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30}:\n\n        <awm_tool_call>\n        {\"name\": \"call_tool\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"create_applicant\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Alice\\\", \\\"age\\\": 30}\"}}\n        </awm_tool_call>\n\n        - Reading that call: name = \"call_tool\", arguments.tool_name = \"create_applicant\", arguments.arguments = the STRING \"{\\\"name\\\": \\\"Alice\\\", \\\"age\\\": 30}\".\n        - A tool that takes no arguments: {\"name\": \"call_tool\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"list_camps\", \"arguments\": \"{}\"}}.\n        - Do NOT fall back to any native/DSML function-calling syntax in this step: the harness REJECTS the whole message (the environment never sees it) and replies with a FORMAT ERROR, which only wastes your steps.\n\n\n        STRICT FORMAT REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL — read carefully):\n        - This is a PLAIN-TEXT environment: there is NO native function-calling API. You simulate tool calls by outputting the \"<awm_tool_call>...</awm_tool_call>\" tag yourself.\n        - Your tool call MUST be exactly the \"<awm_tool_call>{\"name\": ..., \"arguments\": ...}</awm_tool_call>\" tag shown above. Any OTHER syntax (DSML markers, \"<final_tool_call>\", \"<invoke>\"/\"<parameter>\" tags, or a leading \"response\" text) will NOT be recognized as a tool call.\n        - If your step is not exactly \"<awm_tool_call>...</awm_tool_call>\" or \"<final_answer>...</final_answer>\", it will be treated as the end of the task and you will FAIL.\n        - Emit ONLY ONE tag per step, and nothing else (no surrounding prose, no markdown fences).\n\n         FINAL ANSWER RULES (CRITICAL):\n         - If the task asks to search, list, find, compare, calculate, or return any information, your final_answer MUST contain that information. Do not say that no return value is needed.\n         - A successful tool response is not itself the final answer. You must restate the relevant result in final_answer.\n         - Use the following no-return sentence ONLY when the task exclusively changes database state and explicitly requests no report or returned information:\n        <final_answer>This task requires no return value. I have completed the task.</final_answer>\n\n        Stopping rule (IMPORTANT):\n        - You have at most 15 steps to complete the task. If you cannot finish within 15 steps, it will be counted as a failure, so work efficiently and avoid wasting steps.\n        - <final_answer> also consumes one step.\n\n        Example #1 (list tools):\n        <awm_tool_call>\n        {\"name\": \"list_tools\", \"arguments\": null}\n        </awm_tool_call>\n\n        Example #2 (query tool detail):\n        <awm_tool_call>\n        {\"name\": \"get_tool_detail_of\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"get_weather\"}}\n        </awm_tool_call>\n\n        Example #3 (call tool):\n        <awm_tool_call>\n        {\"name\": \"call_tool\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"get_weather\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Beijing\\\"}\"}}\n        </awm_tool_call>","role":"system"},{"content":"View the current available balance and last 5 transactions for the Chase Total Checking account ending in 4321.","role":"user"},{"content":"<awm_tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"list_tools\", \"arguments\": null}\n</awm_tool_call>","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool response:\nAvailable MCP Tools (1 tools):\n================================================================================\n\n1. get_account_summary\n   Description: Retrieve the current available balance and last 5 transactions for the specified Chase Total Checking account.","role":"tool"},{"content":"<awm_tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_tool_detail_of\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"get_account_summary\"}}\n</awm_tool_call>","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool response:\nTool: get_account_summary\nDescription: Retrieve the current available balance and last 5 transactions for the specified Chase Total Checking account.\nRequires authentication as the account owner.\nParameters:\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"account_number_last4\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"title\": \"Account Number Last4\",\n          \"description\": \"\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"account_number_last4\"\n      ]\n    }","role":"tool"},{"content":"<awm_tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"call_tool\", \"arguments\": {\"tool_name\": \"get_account_summary\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"account_number_last4\\\": \\\"4321\\\"}\"}}\n</awm_tool_call>","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Tool response:\n{\"account\":{\"id\":1,\"account_type\":\"checking\",\"account_number_la